<title>GERMANY: E.German Oct industry output falls 2.7 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E.German Oct industry output falls 2.7 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the</p>
<p>following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Oct 96    Sept 96	Oct 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  -2.7	 -2.6	  -2.7</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +2.7	 +2.7	   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     138.9	142.7	 135.3</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbnk statistics.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Oct 96	    Sept 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   151.7	-4.2     158.4	 -2.2</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    184.4	unch     184.4	 -5.3</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   125.4	-4.1     130.7	 -5.7</p>
<p> Energy output	     84.6	-2.5	86.7	 -2.0</p>
<p> Construction	     201.3	+1.2     198.9	 -4.1</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with July/Aug 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 -1.0</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>Two month comparison Sept/Oct 96 with Sept/Oct 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +2.8</p>
<p> Mining					-7.0</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +7.5</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	 +7.5</p>
<p>		Capital goods		+3.5</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	  -1.4</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	    +14.5</p>
<p> Energy output			     -0.5</p>
<p> Construction				-3.5</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-26097150</p>
